     1                          ; ============================================================
     2                          ; sprites.asm
     3                          ; Sprite data pool - 36 blocks (VIC sprite pointers #33-68),
     4                          ; 64 bytes each (63 bytes of pixel data + 1 unused byte).
     5                          ; Source: decompressed image $0840-$1140.
     6                          ; Confirmed by rendering (see reference/sprite_sheet.png):
     7                          ; monster and player sprites matching the M$/MN DATA tables
     8                          ; in the BASIC source (spider, centipede, worm, dragon, etc).
     9                          ; Blocks 33-63 are pointed to directly via POKE 2040..2047.
    10                          ; Blocks 64-68 are unused "template" frames copied into the
    11                          ; active 60-63 slots at runtime for animation.
    12                          ; ============================================================
    13                          
